 | The same pair again | Only the selection changes: no retune, the stop goes on (cheap; the UI asks again on every change) |
 | A new pair | The receiver stays where it is when that channel is still one of the two (a call it holds too), else it tunes the selected one |
 | A signal | Holds the receiver as in a scan, then the wait (`dual_delay_ms`, below). Resume mode stop counts as carrier: a signal never ends the watch |
-| The wait after a signal | The receiver stays on that channel for the reply, and after each dwell there looks at the other channel for one dwell (squelch shut). A digital signal counts by noise or signal strength, just as during a normal scan visit. A signal found there sets its bit in the view's `dual_busy` (the pane shows Busy) and is not played or held: the receiver goes back and the wait goes on. A look starts only if a look and a dwell back fit in what is left of the wait. When the wait ends the watch alternates again, so a busy channel is held then. A look that hears nothing clears the bit, as does the watch's own hop to that channel and a stop. A hold (a signal, the DMR reply window) has no looks |
+| The wait after a signal | The receiver stays on that channel for the reply, and after each dwell there looks at the other channel for one dwell (squelch shut). A digital signal counts by noise or signal strength, just as during a normal scan visit. A carrier found there sets its bit in the view's `dual_busy` (the pane shows Busy) and the receiver goes back. If the digital engine opens voice during the look, that call takes the ordinary receive hold on its channel. A look starts only if a look and a dwell back fit in what is left of the wait. When the wait ends the watch alternates again. A look that hears nothing clears the bit, as does the watch's own hop to that channel and a stop. A hold (a signal, the DMR reply window) has no looks |
 | DMR reply window | Holds the selected channel while it runs (PTT talks there). On the other channel it doesn't |
 | PTT | Tunes the selected channel first if the receiver is on the other, and transmits there. The watch goes on: after the transmission (DMR: after its tail) the selected channel waits (`dual_delay_ms`, with looks at the other), and a reply holds it |
 | Monitor down | Tunes the selected channel first if the receiver is on the other, then acts as without the watch (FM: squelch open; DMR: digital monitor on the release). The watch pauses there while the key is held |
